No interface is up, for `doctor`: `route -n get default` says nothing and
`ipconfig getifaddr en0` answers nothing and exits 1 (as it does with no
address; an empty answer with exit 0 is one the real tool never gives, and the
two implementations read it differently), so detect_iface finds no physical NIC —
NO_PHYSICAL_NETWORK, the reach row reads "over the NIC" with every NIC probe
"-", and only the default-route probe runs (and fails, nothing cans it).
